// `{` after `=>` opens a block, and the advice now says what to do about it.
//
// `1 => { a: 1 }` reads as an arm whose body is a block containing the
// statement `a`, and then the `:` has nowhere to go. The standing advice —
// "expected a line break or `;` here" — is advice that cannot be followed: no
// line break makes that a map. Parentheses do, and now the note says so.
let r = match 1 {
  1 => { a: 1 },
  _ => 0,
}
print(r)
